From: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: en751221: 1024 descriptors on QDMA1 RX ring 0

Every downstream frame the CPU forwards (WiFi through WHNAT, routed LAN)
arrives on QDMA_WAN RX ring 0. When forwarding saturates the CPU the
vendor 512 entries fill: under a CPU-bound load RX_HWI == RX_CPUI was
sampled in nearly every loaded second, and GDM2 dropped frames
(GDMA2_RX_ETHDROPCNT = pon0 rx_dropped) only in those seconds. A WiFi
speed test drops 1000-1600 frames per second at its ~650 Mbit/s peaks and
TCP saws down to ~200 Mbit/s. HW-forwarded traffic at 800 Mbit/s never
touches the ring and drops nothing. ~650 Mbit/s with a 20 ms RTT needs
~1080 packets of buffer.

Signed-off-by: Cristian Papa <pcristian292@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -5548,7 +5548,14 @@
 		cfg->num_channels = 8;
 	} else if (soc->version == econet_en751221 && id == 1) {
 		/* Vendor QDMA_WAN profile. */
-		cfg->num_rx_descs[0] = 512;
+		/*
+		 * lab: every downstream frame the CPU forwards (WiFi, routed
+		 * LAN) arrives on RX ring 0. When forwarding saturates the CPU,
+		 * the vendor's 512 entries fill and GDM2 drops the frames
+		 * (GDMA2_RX_ETHDROPCNT, pon0 rx_dropped): ~650 Mbit/s with a
+		 * 20 ms RTT needs ~1080 packets of buffer, so TCP saws down.
+		 */
+		cfg->num_rx_descs[0] = 1024;
 		cfg->num_rx_descs[1] = 256;
 		cfg->num_tx_descs[0] = 1024;
 		cfg->num_tx_descs[1] = 128;
